abstract: >
  NeuroInsight is a neuroimaging pipeline platform for processing, monitoring,
  and visualizing brain MRI and multimodal data. It supports containerized
  pipelines (FreeSurfer, FastSurfer, fMRIPrep, QSIPrep, XCP-D, MELD Graph, EEG/MNE
  steps) with local Docker, remote SSH, and HPC via SLURM and Apptainer. Transfer
  moves data between Local, HPC, Pennsieve, and XNAT; Jobs submits compute on
  staged paths. All outputs are for research use only; clinical support use is
  solely the user's responsibility (docs/RESEARCH_OUTPUT_USE.md). Developed by
  Philbert Ndagijimana with URMC collaborators; workflows support Radiology and
  Neurology programs. Cohort-scale TRACK-TBI (DoD collaboration:
  University of Rochester and University of Pennsylvania): 600 subjects, two
  timepoints; workflow delivered in the TRACK-TBI DoD technical report
  (docs/TRACK_TBI.md). See docs/ENGINEERING.md and docs/CLINICAL_SUPPORT.md.
